### ==========================================================
### Vector DB Seed Data — 5 checkpoints
### Populate CheckpointEmbedding with realistic past cases
### so future similarity searches have reference material.
### ==========================================================

@server = http://localhost:4004

### insertCheckpointEmbedding for Available Box Check
# @name insertCheckpointEmbedding_POST
### insertCheckpointEmbedding
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/ai/insertCheckpointEmbedding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Available Box Check",
  "resolution": "Fetch all boxes from DIS where Processed = 6 and Verified = true. Compare the total available box count between DIS and PSA. If the counts do not match, identify the specific box numbers that exist in DIS but are missing in PSA, and vice versa. Validate whether the missing boxes were not loaded into PSA, were incorrectly marked as unavailable, or were removed due to downstream processing issues. Reprocess or synchronize the affected box records to ensure both systems contain the same set of available boxes.",
  "discrepancy_data": "{\"PSABoxNumber\":null,\"PSAStatus\":null,\"DISBoxNumber\":\"BOX-0002\",\"DISProcessed\":\"6\",\"Matched\":false}"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------
###   Shipped BOL Check — totalUnits mismatch
### Fields: Blading / totalUnits / totalVolume / totalBoxes
### SOT: DIS (tblShipped) vs PSA (shipmentReport, boxforbol)
### ---------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/ai/insertCheckpointEmbedding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Shipped BOL Check",
  "resolution": "**Root Cause:** BOL-1000012 had 1 bleed unit added manually in DIS after the daily PSA sync ran, so PSA totalUnits was 1 short.\n\n**Resolution:** Triggered manual PSA sync job (Job ID: PSA_SYNC_BOL). Confirmed totalUnits, totalVolume, and totalBoxes now match between DIS and PSA. Flagged the manual DIS update to Ops for future prevention.",
  "discrepancy_data": "[{\"Blading\":\"BOL-1000012\",\"PSATotalUnits\":4,\"PSATotalVolume\":52.5,\"PSATotalBoxes\":2,\"DISTotalUnits\":5,\"DISTotalVolume\":52.5,\"DISTotalBoxes\":2,\"MatchedUnits\":\"No\",\"MatchedVolume\":\"Yes\",\"MatchedBoxes\":\"Yes\"}]"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------
###   Shipped BOL Check — totalVolume + totalBoxes mismatch
### ---------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/ai/insertCheckpointEmbedding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Shipped BOL Check",
  "resolution": "**Root Cause:** BOL-1000015 involved a box split at shipment. DIS recorded the split as 2 separate boxes but PSA still showed the original 1 box, causing volume and box count mismatches.\n\n**Resolution:** Investigated the box split log in DIS, manually reconciled BOX-0089A and BOX-0089B into PSA boxforbol. Re-ran PSA aggregation. Now all three aggregates match.",
  "discrepancy_data": "[{\"Blading\":\"BOL-1000015\",\"PSATotalUnits\":3,\"PSATotalVolume\":34.2,\"PSATotalBoxes\":1,\"DISTotalUnits\":3,\"DISTotalVolume\":68.4,\"DISTotalBoxes\":2,\"MatchedUnits\":\"Yes\",\"MatchedVolume\":\"No\",\"MatchedBoxes\":\"No\"}]"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------
###  Shipped Consignee per BOL Check — reconsignment
### Fields: Blading / Customer(DIS) / consigneenumber(PSA)
### SOT: PSA (shipmentReport) vs DIS (tblShipped)
### ---------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/ai/insertCheckpointEmbedding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Shipped Consignee per BOL Check",
  "resolution": "**Root Cause:** BOL-1000021 was reconsigned in PSA from CUST-4501 to CUST-4780 after the DIS record was created. The reconsignment event was not propagated back to DIS.\n\n**Resolution:** Confirmed the reconsignment log in PSA. Updated the Customer field in DIS tblShipped to CUST-4780 to match PSA (source of truth). Documented that reconsignments require a manual DIS update until auto-sync is implemented.",
  "discrepancy_data": "[{\"Blading\":\"BOL-1000021\",\"PSAConsigneeNumber\":\"CUST-4780\",\"DISCustomer\":\"CUST-4501\",\"Matched\":false}]"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------
###  Shipped Consignee per BOL Check — manual DIS update
### ---------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/ai/insertCheckpointEmbedding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Shipped Consignee per BOL Check",
  "resolution": "**Root Cause:** BOL-1000023 had a data-entry typo in DIS (CUST-390 instead of CUST-3900). No reconsignment event was found in PSA.\n\n**Resolution:** Corrected the Customer value in DIS tblShipped to CUST-3900. Re-ran the consignee comparison and confirmed match with PSA. Escalated the typo to DIS Ops team for training feedback.",
  "discrepancy_data": "[{\"Blading\":\"BOL-1000023\",\"PSAConsigneeNumber\":\"CUST-3900\",\"DISCustomer\":\"CUST-390\",\"Matched\":false}]"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------
###  Part Number per BOL Check — reconsignment change
### Fields: Blading / partnumber
### SOT: PSA (shipmentReport) vs CCC (Shipped_tblBOLPartNumber)
### ---------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/ai/insertCheckpointEmbedding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Part Number per BOL Check",
  "resolution": "**Root Cause:** BOL-1000031 was reconsigned in PSA and the part number changed from PN-A1024 to PN-A1099. The change was not reflected in CCC Shipped_tblBOLPartNumber.\n\n**Resolution:** Verified the reconsignment audit trail in PSA. Manually updated the partnumber value in CCC Shipped_tblBOLPartNumber to PN-A1099. Match confirmed.",
  "discrepancy_data": "[{\"Blading\":\"BOL-1000031\",\"PSAPartNumber\":\"PN-A1099\",\"CCCPartNumber\":\"PN-A1024\",\"Matched\":false}]"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------
###  Part Number per BOL Check — manual CCC edit
### ---------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/ai/insertCheckpointEmbedding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Part Number per BOL Check",
  "resolution": "**Root Cause:** BOL-1000034 had a manual part number update in CCC (PN-B2050 -> PN-B2050X) that was not authorized and did not follow reconsignment flow in PSA.\n\n**Resolution:** Reverted the CCC value back to PN-B2050 to match PSA (source of truth). Raised a ticket with CCC access team to review who applied the manual change. No PSA changes needed.",
  "discrepancy_data": "[{\"Blading\":\"BOL-1000034\",\"PSAPartNumber\":\"PN-B2050\",\"CCCPartNumber\":\"PN-B2050X\",\"Matched\":false}]"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------
###  Material Information Check — missing MaterialDesc in PSA
### Fields: Boxnumber / Bleednumber / Materialdesc
### SOT: DIS/ODS (vw_boxed) vs PSA (BOXFORBOL, prod_vw_boxed)
### ---------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/ai/insertCheckpointEmbedding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Material Information Check",
  "resolution": "**Root Cause:** BOX-0141 existed in PSA BOXFORBOL but MaterialDesc was NULL. Cross-check with prod_vw_boxed showed the material was populated correctly, meaning the propagation from prod_vw_boxed to BOXFORBOL failed silently.\n\n**Resolution:** Re-ran the material propagation job for BOX-0141. MaterialDesc now populated as 'Immune Globulin 10% 50mL'. Verified across all 3 units in the box. Filed an issue to add job failure alerting.",
  "discrepancy_data": "[{\"Boxnumber\":\"BOX-0141\",\"Bleednumber\":\"BLD-8801\",\"PSAMaterialDesc\":null,\"ODSMaterialDesc\":\"Immune Globulin 10% 50mL\",\"Matched\":false}]"
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------
###  Material Information Check — mismatched MaterialDesc
### ---------------------------------------------------------
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/ai/insertCheckpointEmbedding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Material Information Check",
  "resolution": "**Root Cause:** BOX-0157 had MaterialDesc 'Albumin 25% 100mL' in PSA but ODS vw_boxed showed 'Albumin 25% 50mL'. Upstream ODS had a corrected material spec update that never propagated to PSA.\n\n**Resolution:** Confirmed ODS is source of truth. Updated PSA BOXFORBOL MaterialDesc to 'Albumin 25% 50mL'. Also validated all units within BOX-0157 (3 units total) are consistent. Root cause: missed nightly sync window on 2026-07-18.",
  "discrepancy_data": "[{\"Boxnumber\":\"BOX-0157\",\"Bleednumber\":\"BLD-9012\",\"PSAMaterialDesc\":\"Albumin 25% 100mL\",\"ODSMaterialDesc\":\"Albumin 25% 50mL\",\"Matched\":false}]"
}


